    "about": "Connor has refereed in the ECFA since 2023. Away from football, he plays lawn bowls and appeared on Countdown around 2024.\n\nHe enjoys the league’s competitive football alongside the banter and laughs with players. His biggest frustration is pitches he considers playable being called off by Edinburgh Leisure without a referee inspection.\n\nHis largest-crowd occasion was Haddington against Jeanfield in the East of Scotland Premier, when both sides were joint top early the previous season.\n\nAs a Hearts supporter, Tynecastle Park is his favourite venue to have refereed at, although he also enjoyed Easter Road.",
